Subject: [PATCH] bzip2: silence -Wsign-compare for the vendored code

The vendored bzip2 code (archival/libarchive/bz/*) is kept identical
to upstream; its uint/int loop counters trip -Wsign-compare from
our -Wextra policy. Keep the code pristine and silence only that
diagnostic via #pragma in the busybox wrapper TU.
diff --git a/archival/bzip2.c b/archival/bzip2.c
index bce13cf..67eec2a 100644
--- a/archival/bzip2.c
+++ b/archival/bzip2.c
@@ -6,6 +6,10 @@
  * See README and LICENSE files in bz/ directory for more information
  * about bzip2 library code.
  */
+/* The vendored bzip2 code below is kept identical to upstream; its
+ * uint/int loop counters trip -Wsign-compare (from -Wextra).  Keep the
+ * code pristine and silence only that diagnostic for this TU. */
+#pragma GCC diagnostic ignored "-Wsign-compare"
 //config:config BZIP2
 //config:	bool "bzip2 (16 kb)"
 //config:	default y
